      "description": "Watch Cagliari vs Arezzo highlights and goals from Coppa Italia on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 14, 2026. The Coppa Italia campaign kicked off with a high-stakes encounter on August 14, 2026 , as Cagliari played host to a resilient Arezzo side. With both teams desperate to advance in the prestigious knockout competition, the atmosphere was electric from the opening whistle. Deiola Breaks the Deadlock Cagliari signaled their intent early on, coming agonizingly close to an opener in the 15th minute when both Alessandro Deiola and Paul Mendy struck the post in quick succession. The pressure eventually told in the 18th minute when Deiola was fouled inside the box by Alessandro Renzi . The captain took responsibility himself, stepping up to the spot and calmly slotting a right-footed shot into the bottom left corner to give his side the lead in the 23rd minute. Arezzo refused to be intimidated and grew into the game as the first half drew to a close. They nearly found an equalizer in stoppage time when Luca Chierico met a cross with a powerful header, but Cagliari goalkeeper Elia Caprile produced a stunning save in the top right corner to preserve the advantage heading into the break. Defensive Resilience and Late Scares The second half saw Arezzo throw everything forward in search of a way back. Mattia Sala tested Caprile again in the 62nd minute, while a VAR review shortly after denied the visitors a penalty, keeping the tension at a boiling point. Despite the introduction of fresh legs like Daniel Maldini and Matteo Prati , Cagliari struggled to find a second goal to kill off the tie, with Arezzo goalkeeper Alessandro Nunziante making vital saves from Mattia Felici and Gennaro Borrelli . As the clock ticked deep into ten minutes of added time, Arezzo launched one final assault. A header from Julián Illanes was bravely blocked by the Sardo defense, and Andrea Cagnano sent a late effort high and wide. After a grueling battle, Cagliari held firm to secure their place in the next round, surviving a spirited challenge from their lower-league opponents."
